    #          output row followed at once by its input row (P1 ruling 3); and
    #          fixture.b, the keep pair whose input the record says LibreOffice
    #          refused, with no row at all (the "keep pair whose input LibreOffice
    #          refused" case of "P1");
    #     part 8 P2's cases rerun, each exit 2, one "error: " line, no stdout, no
    #     list: L1 a run directory with a missing host output; L2 a record whose
    #     hash the kept file does not match; L3 a keep directory with an odd file;
    #     L4 a record that does not name exactly the keep's pairs; L5 an --out
    #     already there (left untouched);
    #     and this phase's: L6 a --run-plain directory with no summary.host.tsv;
    #     L7 a --run-plain directory whose output is one byte longer than the
    #     summary's out_bytes (P1 ruling 1), and L7r the same on --run; L8 a
    #     --run-plain directory under another corpus root (P1 ruling 4); L9 a
    #     manifest row one column short, which the base's script let escape as a
    #     traceback with exit 1 (specs/0015 P2 verification ruling 4): here exit
    #     2 and one "error: " line, with the base's script run on the same
    #     layout as the control that the change is what catches it; L10 the base
    #     script's list mode under the same umask, the control for L0's mode.
    # (P) scripts/excel-check-open.ps1, which no PowerShell runs here (P1
    #     ruling 11): it is ASCII and holds no absolute path, by a grep with a
    #     control for each form: a copy with one non-ASCII byte planted, and
    #     copies with a drive-letter path, a UNC path, a root-anchored path and a
    #     home-relative path planted, each found by the same command form.
    #
    # ATTEMPT 3, after independent check 1's F4: the scripts under test run from
    # git-show copies in <scratch>/w/scripts, not the main tree. Nothing else changed.
    #
    # WRITTEN FOR M2 part 1 P1 from part 8 P2's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m1p8-p2/negative.log). From it: lines 1 to 3, the shape greps
