    # lines, the counting controls, the scripts checked against the phase commit,
    # and family L's generator, helpers and cases L0 to L5. What differs, and why:
    #  1. The phase, the log directory and the subjects are M2 part 1 P1's.
    #  2. The generated summaries carry out_bytes, which the script now reads
    #     (P1 ruling 1); L0 gains the --run-plain directory and the input row;
    #     the counts line is the script's new one.
    #  3. Families S and R are dropped: this phase changes scripts/lo-check.sh
    #     and the runner not at all, and scripts/edit-open-check.sh by one
    #     heading string, which run.log's record check reads. No binary is built
    #     and no container runs.
    #  4. Family P is new ("P1": the PowerShell script's grep with a control).
    #  5. The status checks print the status lines themselves (specs/0015 P2
    #     verification ruling 2) and allow planning's uncommitted spec and this
    #     phase's logs and two record pairs.
    #
    # Usage: m2p1-p1-negative.sh <phase commit> > <scratch file>; the caller moves
